From 51d6a0759debc0e819f1583b690e0f2c4f22e0bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Philip Mueller <claude@philipmueller.ch>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 13:52:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 30/31] fix(token-capture): keep lineage after a tool call with
 unparseable arguments

OpenCode (AI SDK tool-call repair) does not echo a tool call whose
arguments are not JSON as served. It keeps the call id and rewrites the
call as `invalid` with {"tool": <name>, "error": "Invalid input for tool
<name>: JSON parsing failed: ..."}. The served call hashed
(id, name, raw arguments), the echo (id, "invalid", error object), so
the next call matched no parent and every later call of the rollout
was poisoned (unresolved_parent).

A tool call with an id whose arguments are not JSON now hashes a marker
in place of its arguments, and the `invalid` echo of a JSON parse
failure hashes as the call it repairs: same id, the named tool, the
marker. The served tokens stay what the policy generated. Other
`invalid` calls, schema-validation echoes (arguments were JSON) and
calls without an id hash as before. FINGERPRINT_VERSION 4 -> 5.

Seen on Apertus 2 with OpenCode 1.17.11: 1 of 16 rollouts lost, 11
calls poisoned. Replaying that run's 16 captured rollouts, 64 of 74
follow-up calls found their parent before, 74 of 74 after, none
ambiguous.

Signed-off-by: Philip Mueller <claude@philipmueller.ch>
